    "reason": "While 往来 (ōrai) can mean 'traffic' (as indicated by JMdict glosses 'coming and going, traffic'), it is not the most common or natural term a general learner would expect for the English concept of 'traffic', especially in the context of vehicle traffic or general road conditions. 往来 often emphasizes the act of 'coming and going' or 'passage'. The more standard and widely used term for 'traffic' (e.g., road traffic, traffic laws, traffic jams) in Japanese is 交通 (kōtsū).",
